Z||000000||falconhulk||08-21-2001||02:46 PM||||There are 2 pipes coming off the rear engine/trunk wall.  One of these pipes goes from the wall to just before the coil.  The other is about 1 foot to the right.They are both bolted to the wall.  Are these some kind of air tubes?  Do they do some kind of cooling?  I have looked throug the Haynes and the Chilton manual and they say nothing. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||08-21-2001||03:04 PM||||Yes they are cooling pipes for the coil and alternator. There is a fan in the passenger side of the trunk behind the carpet. It operates in unison with the radiator fan.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 08-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||08-21-2001||03:05 PM||||I just found out what those pipes were a few months back .One is used to cool the alternater  And the other is to cool the coil and ther is a fan that is tucked away in the trunk compartment in back.passenger side I have not looked or found it yet .hope this answers your question<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||falconhulk||08-21-2001||03:19 PM||||I kind of figured what they were but just wanted to make sure no one broke something off of my car before I got it!!!  lol.  Thanks guys.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mickey_Moose||08-21-2001||06:22 PM||||Yes they are cooling pipes, and the fan is located on the passenger side of the rear trunk. Not on 88's<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
